<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Morocco</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Moroccan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Morocco is a country in north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> with Atlantic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coasts. It was the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a>, whose capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marrakesh">Marrakesh</a>. In 1591 a Moroccan army destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a>, and Morocco's trade routes linked it to the Ghana and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> regions across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/morocco.jpg" alt="Morocco" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Denelson83, Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Morocco.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
